<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">11 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 11 June, from 786 to 2001.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">786 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,240 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasids crush an Alid revolt at the Battle of Fakhkh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Abbasid forces crushed an Alid revolt led by al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/husayn-ibn-ali">Husayn ibn Ali</a>, a descendant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-ali">Hasan ibn Ali</a>, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>; al-Husayn and many of his followers were killed. A survivor, Idris ibn Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a>, fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/idrisid-dynasty">Idrisid dynasty</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-fakhkh">Battle of Fakhkh</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alids">Alids</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">806 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,220 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An Abbasid army sets out from Raqqa to invade Asia Minor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">Caliph</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harun-al-rashid">Harun al-Rashid</a>, far larger than any assembled before, left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raqqa">Raqqa</a>, crossed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus Mountains</a> and invaded Byzantine Cappadocia. The Byzantine losses, including the sack of Herakleia, forced <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikephoros-i">Emperor Nikephoros</a> to seek peace.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1011">1011 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,015 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bari's Greek citizens deliver the city to the Byzantine catepan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Greek citizens of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a> rose against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> rebels led by Melus and delivered the city to Basil Mesardonites, the Byzantine catepan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, who entered it and re-established Byzantine authority.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bari">Bari</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1509">1509 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">517 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VIII marries Catherine of Aragon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Weeks after his accession, Henry married his brother Arthur's widow at Greenwich. Their failure to produce a surviving son later led Henry to break with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1776">1776 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">250 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress appoints a committee to draft a declaration of independence</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a>, John Adams, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-franklin">Benjamin Franklin</a>, Roger Sherman and Robert Livingston formed the Committee of Five. Jefferson wrote the first draft.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thích Quảng Đức burns himself to death in Saigon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Buddhist monk set himself alight at a busy junction to protest the Diem government's treatment of Buddhists. Malcolm Browne's photograph shocked the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1963">1963 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">63 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">George Wallace stands in the schoolhouse door</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alabama">Alabama</a>'s governor blocked the entrance to the University of Alabama to stop two Black students enrolling, then stood aside when federalised Guard troops arrived. Kennedy addressed the nation on civil rights that night.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2001">2001 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">25 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Timothy McVeigh is executed for the Oklahoma City bombing</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">McVeigh was put to death by lethal injection in Terre Haute, Indiana. It was the first federal execution in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> since 1963.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li></ol>
